{"id":"G0091","name":"Silence","aliases":["Whisper Spider"],"url":"https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0091","summary":"Silence is a financially motivated threat actor targeting financial institutions in different countries. The group was first seen in June 2016. Their main targets reside in Russia, Ukraine, Belarus, Azerbaijan, Poland and Kazakhstan. They compromised various banking systems, including the Russian Central Bank's Automated Workstation Client, ATMs, and card processing.","summaryCites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"}],"procedures":[{"id":"T1027.010","text":"Silence has used environment variable string substitution for obfuscation.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"}]},{"id":"T1036.005","text":"Silence has named its backdoor \"WINWORD.exe\".","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1055","text":"Silence has injected a DLL library containing a Trojan into the fwmain32.exe process.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1070.004","text":"Silence has deleted artifacts, including scheduled tasks, communicates files from the C2 and other logs.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1078","text":"Silence has used compromised credentials to log on to other systems and escalate privileges.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1112","text":"Silence can create, delete, or modify a specified Registry key or value.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1218.001","text":"Silence has weaponized CHM files in their phishing campaigns.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Aug 2019","url":"https://www.group-ib.com/resources/threat-research/silence_2.0.going_global.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1553.002","text":"Silence has used a valid certificate to sign their primary loader Silence.Downloader (aka TrueBot).","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Aug 2019","url":"https://www.group-ib.com/resources/threat-research/silence_2.0.going_global.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1588.002","text":"Silence has obtained and modified versions of publicly-available tools like Empire and PsExec.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Aug 2019","url":"https://www.group-ib.com/resources/threat-research/silence_2.0.going_global.pdf"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"}]},{"id":"T1566.001","text":"Silence has sent emails with malicious DOCX, CHM, LNK and ZIP attachments.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1053.005","text":"Silence has used scheduled tasks to stage its operation.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"}]},{"id":"T1059.001","text":"Silence has used PowerShell to download and execute payloads.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1059.003","text":"Silence has used Windows command-line to run commands.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1059.005","text":"Silence has used VBS scripts.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"}]},{"id":"T1059.007","text":"Silence has used JS scripts.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"}]},{"id":"T1072","text":"Silence has used RAdmin, a remote software tool used to remotely control workstations and ATMs.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1106","text":"Silence has leveraged the Windows API, including using CreateProcess() or ShellExecute(), to perform a variety of tasks.","cites":[{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1204.002","text":"Silence attempts to get users to launch malicious attachments delivered via spearphishing emails.","cites":[{"name":"Cyber Forensicator Silence Jan 2019","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https://cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"},{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1569.002","text":"Silence has used Winexe to install a service on the remote system.","cites":[{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1547.001","text":"Silence has used `HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run`, `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run`, and the Startup folder to establish persistence.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1003.001","text":"Silence has used the Farse6.1 utility (based on Mimikatz) to extract credentials from lsass.exe.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1018","text":"Silence has used Nmap to scan the corporate network, build a network topology, and identify vulnerable hosts.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1021.001","text":"Silence has used RDP for lateral movement.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1113","text":"Silence can capture victim screen activity.","cites":[{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1125","text":"Silence has been observed making videos of victims to observe bank employees day to day activities.","cites":[{"name":"SecureList Silence Nov 2017","url":"https://securelist.com/the-silence/83009/"},{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1090.002","text":"Silence has used ProxyBot, which allows the attacker to redirect traffic from the current node to the backconnect server via Sock4\\Socks5.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1105","text":"Silence has downloaded additional modules and malware to victim’s machines.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]},{"id":"T1571","text":"Silence has used port 444 when sending data about the system from the client to the server.","cites":[{"name":"Group IB Silence Sept 2018","url":"https://go.group-ib.com/report-silence-en?_gl=1*d1bh3a*_ga*MTIwMzM5Mzc5MS4xNjk4OTI5NzY4*_ga_QMES53K3Y2*MTcwNDcyMjU2OS40LjEuMTcwNDcyMzU1Mi41My4wLjA."}]}],"observables":[{"kind":"file","value":"fwmain32.exe","tech":"T1055"},{"kind":"file","value":"lsass.exe","tech":"T1003.001"},{"kind":"file","value":"WINWORD.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"registry","value":"HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run","tech":"T1547.001"},{"kind":"registry","value":"HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run","tech":"T1547.001"}],"sources":[{"name":"Crowdstrike GTR2020 Mar 2020","url":"https://go.crowdstrike.